## 7. OUTCOME FEEDBACK LOOP

### 7.1 The Flywheel (Inspired by Maiat)

Maiat's core insight: every trust query feeds the ML model. More queries → better predictions →
more trustworthy scores → more queries. x204 adopts this with the feedback endpoint:

```
POST /x204/feedback
{
  "receiptId": "rcpt-a1b2c3d4",
  "outcome": "success",         // success | partial | failure
  "qualityScore": 9,            // 1-10
  "latencyAcceptable": true,
  "notes": "Fast, accurate data"
}

Response:
{
  "credited": 0.1,              // Reporter earns credits
  "providerTrustDelta": +0.02,  // Provider's score updated
  "totalFeedbacks": 1248,       // System-wide feedback count
  "feedbackWeight": 3.0         // Your feedback weight (based on YOUR trust)
}
```

### 7.2 Feedback Weighting (Anti-Sybil, from Maiat)

Not all feedback is equal. Weight depends on the reporter's own history:

| Reporter Profile                           | Weight |
|--------------------------------------------|--------|
| New agent (< 10 transactions)              | 0.5x   |
| Active agent (10-100 transactions)         | 1.0x   |
| High-volume agent (100+ transactions)      | 2.0x   |
| Agent with spend history > $10             | 3.0x   |
| Agent with attestation history (EAS/AID)   | 5.0x   |

This kills Sybil attacks: creating 100 fake agents to boost a provider's score costs real money
because low-trust agents' feedback barely counts.

### 7.3 Real-Time Trust Alerts (Inspired by Maiat Sentinel)

When a provider's trust score drops significantly, all active consumers are notified:

```
GET /x204/alerts?did=did:clawnet:zXYZ...
SSE stream:

event: trust_degradation
data: {
  "provider": "did:clawnet:zXYZ...",
  "previousScore": 87,
  "currentScore": 62,
  "trigger": "3 consecutive failures reported",
  "severity": "warning",
  "recommendation": "Consider alternative providers"
}
```

Agents polling the heartbeat endpoint also receive trust alerts inline.

